From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:24:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(installer): leave other apps' splits beside a loose
 APK out of its install

A loose APK takes the split_*.apk and config.*.apk files in its folder as
its companions. In a shared folder such as Downloads those include other
apps' splits (a config.arm64_v8a.apk kept from an earlier bundle), and
the install then failed on their signatures or the cluster check, though
nothing of the APK being installed was wrong.

Keep only the companions whose manifest names the base's package and log
the others. A companion of the same package is still checked as before,
so a same-package split with another signer is still refused
(InstallerSigningTest), and an archive's entries are not filtered.

SplitPackageContractTest puts another package's split beside an installed
base and expects the install to be unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0185vQkPNo1ENZ3Mi9zALKd2
